WineCellar API
A Spring Boot REST application built as part of an internal transition from Automation QA to Java Backend Developer and
designed to demonstrate production-ready backend skills.
The application manages wines and wineries, exposing a clean REST API with full CRUD support,
pagination, validation, error handling, and comprehensive test coverage.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Purpose
This project was built to:
Demonstrate practical Spring Boot backend development
Apply clean architecture and layering
Enforce correct REST semantics (status codes, error contracts, pagination)

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tech Stack

- Java 17
- Spring Boot
- Spring Web (REST)
- Spring Data JPA (Hibernate)
- Spring Security
- H2 (in-memory database for tests)
- OpenAPI / Swagger (springdoc)
- JUnit 5, Mockito, MockMvc

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Domain Model

Winery
id
name
country
Uniqueness rule: (name, country)

Wine
id
name
wineYear
country
price
winery
Uniqueness rule: (name, wineYear, winery)

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REST API Overview

Wineries

POST /api/wineries – create winery

GET /api/wineries – list all wineries

GET /api/wineries/paged – paginated & sorted wineries

GET /api/wineries/{id} – get winery by id

PUT /api/wineries/{id} – update winery

DELETE /api/wineries/{id} – delete winery

GET /api/wineries/{id}/wines – list wines for winery

GET /api/wineries/{id}/wines/paged – paged wines for winery

Wines

POST /api/wines – create wine

GET /api/wines – list wines (optional country filter)

GET /api/wines/paged – paginated & sorted wines

GET /api/wines/{id} – get wine by id

PUT /api/wines/{id} – update wine

DELETE /api/wines/{id} – delete wine

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pagination & Sorting

All paged endpoints support:

page (default 0)

size (default 5)

sort (default name)

Example:

GET /api/wineries/paged?page=1&size=5&sort=name

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Error Handling

Centralized error handling using @RestControllerAdvice.

Error responses:

400 Bad Request – validation errors

404 Not Found – missing resources

409 Conflict – domain conflicts (duplicates)

Example error payload:

{
  "error": "Wine already exists: Feteasca Neagra (2022) for winery 1",
  "timestamp": "2025-09-25T12:34:56"
}

Domain Exceptions

NotFoundException

ConflictException

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Transactions

@Transactional applied at service class level

Read operations use @Transactional(readOnly = true)

Write operations are atomic and consistent

Optimistic locking (@Version) prevents lost updates; update requests include version, stale updates return 409 Conflict.

This follows Spring/JPA best practices and avoids hidden transactional behavior.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Security

The API is secured using Spring Security with HTTP Basic authentication in a stateless configuration.

Roles:
- USER – read-only access
- ADMIN – full write access

Authorization rules:
- GET endpoints: USER or ADMIN
- POST / PUT / DELETE endpoints: ADMIN only

Authorization is enforced at the service layer using @PreAuthorize to ensure
business rules are protected regardless of controller entry point.

Security behavior is verified through integration tests covering:
- 401 Unauthorized (unauthenticated requests)
- 403 Forbidden (insufficient role)
- Successful access for authorized users

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Testing Strategy

Unit Tests
Service-level tests using Mockito
Cover:
happy paths
not-found scenarios
conflict scenarios
repository interaction verification

Integration Tests
@SpringBootTest + MockMvc
Cover:
full REST API behavior
validation
pagination & sorting
error handling
uniqueness constraints

